# Story 16: Raw Mode Escape Hatch (40s)
# Hook: Stuck in vim inside rysh? Ctrl+O is your escape hatch.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-16-raw-mode.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 10

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Ctrl+O is the escape hatch from raw mode.

[00:03.0 --> 00:06.0]
Start rysh in shell mode.

[00:06.0 --> 00:12.0]
Open vim -- rysh enters raw mode automatically.

[00:12.0 --> 00:15.0]
Press i for insert mode and type some text.

[00:15.0 --> 00:21.0]
Type normally -- all keys go to vim.

[00:21.0 --> 00:24.0]
Press Escape to return to vim normal mode.

[00:24.0 --> 00:29.0]
Now press Ctrl+O. This is the escape hatch -- it breaks out of raw mode into prefix mode.

[00:29.0 --> 00:33.0]
You're in prefix mode now. You could detach with d, switch panes, or do anything else. Press Escape to cancel and return to raw mode.

[00:33.0 --> 00:37.0]
Back in vim. Quit with :q! to discard changes.

[00:37.0 --> 00:40.0]
Ctrl+O -- your safety net when running TUI apps in rysh.

